1
00:00:00,00 --> 00:00:02,07
- The Hooks were first introduced in 2018.

2
00:00:02,07 --> 00:00:03,09
They have been a new additions

3
00:00:03,09 --> 00:00:07,04
to the React library since the version 16.8.

4
00:00:07,04 --> 00:00:09,09
The Hooks give developers the ability

5
00:00:09,09 --> 00:00:11,04
to create stateful components,

6
00:00:11,04 --> 00:00:13,04
and use other React features

7
00:00:13,04 --> 00:00:14,07
without having to write a class.

8
00:00:14,07 --> 00:00:17,02
In other words, Hooks are functions

9
00:00:17,02 --> 00:00:19,08
that lets you hook into the React states

10
00:00:19,08 --> 00:00:22,05
and lifecycle features from a function components.

11
00:00:22,05 --> 00:00:24,01
And so the React API provides

12
00:00:24,01 --> 00:00:26,05
with a few built-in hooks like useState.

13
00:00:26,05 --> 00:00:29,05
useState is a React Hook that lets you add

14
00:00:29,05 --> 00:00:32,04
and store local state variables in a components.

15
00:00:32,04 --> 00:00:34,07
And this is how the syntax looks like.

16
00:00:34,07 --> 00:00:36,07
Whenever you call useState in a component,

17
00:00:36,07 --> 00:00:38,07
it returns an array, with first,

18
00:00:38,07 --> 00:00:41,07
a variable and a function, to update the state.

19
00:00:41,07 --> 00:00:44,06
A new state can take a value as a parameter

20
00:00:44,06 --> 00:00:46,07
of any type to set an initial value.

21
00:00:46,07 --> 00:00:50,05
In this module, we cover how to manage the state effectively

22
00:00:50,05 --> 00:00:53,05
in a React project by using the React built-in Hooks.

23
